<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Taga Castle</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Taga-jō</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Taga Castle was a fortified government centre founded in 724 in present-day Tagajō, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miyagi-prefecture">Miyagi Prefecture</a>. It served as the seat of the governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutsu-province">Mutsu Province</a> and of the Chinjufu, the court's military command against the Emishi, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isawa-castle">Isawa Castle</a> took over in the early 9th century. Its site, with the inscribed Taga stele, is a Special Historic Site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/taga-castle.jpg" alt="Taga Castle" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kumamushi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tagajo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
